                    <English>No Vermiculite</English>
                    <French>Pas de Vermiculite</French>
                </Vermiculite>
            </Main>
            <RURComments xml:space="preserve">
                <airSeal>Air sealing beyond the 10% improvement mentioned above will result in more significant savings. This could be difficult to achieve unless performed during other renovation upgrades (walls, ceiling). </airSeal>
                <mainWalls>Upgrading the wall insulation can be quite expensive but result in significant energy savings. It is also a perfect time to perform air sealing and install new windows. Increasing the insulation by a minimum of R-20 will be eligible for a Good Energy Rebate. </mainWalls>
                <windows>Replacing windows can be quite expensive but focusing on North facing windows and windows in rooms where you spend significant time will increase the comfort and save money on heating costs. There is currently a $100 rebate on new Energy Star Zone 3 windows. </windows>
                <HotWaterSystem>Installing a drain water heat recovery can be quite simple and affordable. The actual annual energy savings is dependant on the length and temperature of showering. They are also eligible for a Good Energy Rebate. </HotWaterSystem>
                <HeatingSystem>I recommend installing a Cold Climate Heat Pump as they are affordable to install and eligible for Good Energy rebates. Heat pumps will operate at 200% efficiency on average over traditional electric heat. I can provide more information on brands and models for our climate if requested. </HeatingSystem>
            </RURComments>
        </Options>
